---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Services — Get Found on ChatGPT, Claude & AI — Rank Labs" description="AI Visibility Report ($499/mo, report only — you implement the fixes) and Full Management ($2,500/mo). GEO scores, AI visibility tracking, blog content, and full site hosting.">

<section class="pt-32 pb-20 px-6">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
    <div class="text-sm text-cyan-300 font-mono mb-4">WHAT WE DO</div>
    <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-6">Get Found on <span class="gradient-text">Every AI Engine</span></h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-muted mb-16 max-w-2xl">
      Two tiers, one mission: make your business the answer when people ask AI. Get the report and make the fixes yourself, or let us do all of it. <a href="/pricing" class="text-cyan-400 hover:underline">Compare pricing →</a>
    </p>

    <!-- GEO vs ASO -->
    <div class="border-t border-white/5 pt-12 mb-16">
      <div class="text-xs text-cyan-300 font-mono mb-2">GEO VS. ASO (AGENTIC SEARCH OPTIMIZATION)</div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-2">Two jobs, <span class="gradient-text">one platform</span></h2>
      <p class="text-muted mb-4 max-w-xl">One site does two different jobs. GEO makes you the answer. ASO makes you the choice.</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted mb-8 max-w-3xl">
        ASO stands for Agentic Search Optimization. We also call it being "agent-ready." GEO (Generative Engine Optimization)
        gets you cited — your business shows up in the answer when someone asks ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini or Perplexity a question.
        ASO gets you chosen: when that same person stops asking questions and asks the AI to do something — "find me a clinic
        near me that's open Thursday and start a booking" — the AI picks the business whose hours, prices, location, service
        list and booking link it can read as data, not the one whose website merely reads well to a human. (Heads up on the
        acronym: in the app world, "ASO" usually means App Store Optimization. That's a completely different thing — we mean
        Agentic Search Optimization.)
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
        <div class="border border-white/10 rounded-xl p-6">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-sm text-cyan-300 mb-1">GEO — Generative Engine Optimization</h3>
          <div class="text-xs text-muted mb-4">get cited in AI answers</div>
          <ul class="space-y-2">
            {[
              { label: 'Structured data / schema markup — so AI knows exactly who you are', shared: true },
              { label: 'Accurate name, address, phone everywhere', shared: true },
              { label: 'AI crawlers allowed to read your site', shared: true },
              { label: 'Clear answers to real customer questions', shared: false },
              { label: 'FAQ content marked up properly', shared: false },
              { label: 'Quotable facts and specifics — prices, timelines, numbers AI can repeat', shared: false },
              { label: 'Reviews and ratings shown on your site, marked up', shared: false },
              { label: 'Author and credential signals', shared: false },
              { label: 'Consistent facts across your whole site', shared: false },
              { label: 'Mentions on sites AI already trusts', shared: false },
              { label: "Topic depth — enough coverage that you're the obvious source", shared: false },
              { label: 'Content freshness and clear publish dates', shared: false },
              { label: 'Plain-language summaries near the top of each page', shared: false },
              { label: 'Local and service-area context', shared: false },
            ].map(b => (
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-sm text-muted">
                {b.shared
                  ? <span class="text-cyan-300 font-mono text-xs shrink-0 mt-0.5">&#8596;</span>
                  : <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 bg-purple-500 rounded-full shrink-0 mt-2"></span>}
                {b.label}
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="border border-white/10 rounded-xl p-6">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-sm text-purple-300 mb-1">ASO / Agent-Ready — Agentic Search Optimization</h3>
          <div class="text-xs text-muted mb-4">get selected by AI agents</div>
          <ul class="space-y-2">
            {[
              { label: 'Structured data / schema markup — extended to actions', shared: true },
              { label: 'Accurate name, address, phone everywhere', shared: true },
              { label: 'Agents allowed through to your booking page — no bot blocks on the path that matters', shared: true },
              { label: 'Machine-readable service menu — every service its own item', shared: false },
              { label: 'Hours of operation in a format machines read', shared: false },
              { label: 'Exact prices, not ranges — "$1,275" beats "affordable"', shared: false },
              { label: 'Appointment availability — can a machine tell you have openings?', shared: false },
              { label: 'A bookable link a machine can open — deep-linkable, works without JavaScript', shared: false },
              { label: 'One unambiguous service location', shared: false },
              { label: 'Verified profiles connected to your site', shared: false },
              { label: 'Booking or enquiry endpoint', shared: false },
              { label: 'Wait time / next-available signal', shared: false },
              { label: 'Confirmation and cancellation terms stated up front', shared: false },
              { label: 'Full transaction capability (advanced — only where a real scheduling system exists)', shared: false },
            ].map(b => (
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-sm text-muted">
                {b.shared
                  ? <span class="text-cyan-300 font-mono text-xs shrink-0 mt-0.5">&#8596;</span>
                  : <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 bg-purple-500 rounded-full shrink-0 mt-2"></span>}
                {b.label}
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-muted mt-4"><span class="text-cyan-300 font-mono">&#8596;</span> marks work that serves both jobs.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Agent-readiness ladder -->
    <div class="border-t border-white/5 pt-12 mb-16">
      <div class="text-xs text-purple-300 font-mono mb-2">AGENT-READINESS LADDER</div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-2">Where you sit on the <span class="gradient-text">agent-readiness ladder</span></h2>
      <p class="text-muted mb-8 max-w-xl">Being agent-ready isn't one switch — it's a ladder, and most businesses are on the bottom rung without knowing it.</p>
      <ul class="space-y-2 mb-6">
        {[
          { level: 'Level 0 — Invisible.', desc: 'No structured data; an AI has to guess your name, address and phone.' },
          { level: 'Level 1 — Identified.', desc: 'A machine can tell who you are and where you are.' },
          { level: 'Level 2 — Screenable.', desc: 'It can answer the routine questions — open hours, prices, quality, service area. This is where you become reliably citable.' },
          { level: 'Level 3 — Reachable.', desc: 'A stable, machine-usable front door to starting a booking or enquiry. The most-skipped rung, and the best value after Level 2.' },
          { level: 'Level 4 — Verifiable.', desc: 'A machine can tell whether you actually have openings. This is where selection is won.' },
          { level: 'Level 5 — Transactable.', desc: 'The agent completes the booking end to end — only worth building on top of a real scheduling system.' },
        ].map(b => (
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-sm text-muted">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 bg-purple-500 rounded-full shrink-0 mt-2"></span>
            <span><span class="text-white font-semibold">{b.level}</span> {b.desc}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted max-w-xl">For almost every business we work with, the highest-return work sits at Levels 3 and 4. We won't sell you Level 5 before you've cleared Level 2.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- AI Visibility Report -->
    <div class="border-t border-white/5 pt-12 mb-16">
      <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-start md:justify-between gap-4 mb-6">
        <div class="min-w-0">
          <div class="text-xs text-purple-300 font-mono mb-2">$499/MO</div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">AI Visibility Report</h2>
          <p class="text-muted mt-2 max-w-xl break-words">Know where you stand on ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, and Perplexity — delivered as a monthly report.</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-muted mt-2"><span class="text-white font-medium">Month-to-month</span>; no long-term contract.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-xl border border-amber-400/40 bg-amber-400/10 p-4 mb-6 max-w-2xl" role="note">
        <div class="text-xs font-mono font-semibold text-amber-300 mb-1">REPORT ONLY</div>
        <p class="text-sm text-white break-words">Rank Labs makes <strong>no changes</strong> to your site. You are responsible for implementing all fixes.</p>
      </div>

      <ul class="space-y-2 mb-6">
        {['GEO score', 'AI-engine visibility tracking (ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, Perplexity)', 'Monthly report'].map(b => (
          <li class="flex items-center gap-3 text-sm text-muted"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 bg-purple-500 rounded-full shrink-0"></span>{b}</li>
        ))}
      </ul>

      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3 sm:items-center">
        <a href="/contact?plan=ai-visibility-report" class="btn-primary">Get the Report</a>
        <a href="/signup?plan=full_management" class="text-sm text-cyan-300 hover:text-cyan-200 font-semibold">Rather have us make the fixes? Upgrade to Full Management →</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Full Management -->
    <div class="border-t border-white/5 pt-12 mb-16">
      <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-start md:justify-between gap-4 mb-6">
        <div>
          <div class="text-xs text-cyan-300 font-mono mb-2">$2,500/MO</div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Full Management</h2>
          <p class="text-muted mt-2 max-w-xl">Weekly SEO audits, keyword & competitor tracking, AI visibility monitoring, and monthly reports — and we implement the fixes. Plus we build, host, and maintain your site. You focus on your business — we handle the rest.</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-muted mt-2"><span class="text-white font-medium">$1,000 migration fee waived with a 6-month contract</span>; otherwise month-to-month plus a $1,000 migration fee.</p>
        </div>
        <span class="text-xs px-3 py-1 bg-purple-500/20 border border-purple-500/40 rounded-full text-purple-300 font-semibold shrink-0 h-fit">MOST POPULAR</span>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-6">
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-sm text-cyan-300 mb-3">Site Hosting & Management</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2">
            {['Global edge hosting (330+ cities)', 'Automatic SSL certificates', 'Global CDN & DDoS protection', 'Unlimited site edits & updates', 'One-click rollbacks & daily backups', 'Site fixes on demand'].map(b => (
              <li class="flex items-center gap-3 text-sm text-muted"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 bg-purple-500 rounded-full shrink-0"></span>{b}</li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-sm text-cyan-300 mb-3">Content Creation</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2">
            {['Weekly blog content (researched & written)', 'Keyword & competitor research per post', '800+ word SEO-optimized drafts', 'Easy approval workflow', 'Scheduled publishing & content calendar', 'Service-area landing pages'].map(b => (
              <li class="flex items-center gap-3 text-sm text-muted"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 bg-purple-500 rounded-full shrink-0"></span>{b}</li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-sm text-cyan-300 mb-3">Local SEO & Listings</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2">
            {['Google Business Profile optimization', 'Business listing management', 'Local schema markup', 'Service-area page strategy', 'City + service keyword targeting', 'Review monitoring & response'].map(b => (
              <li class="flex items-center gap-3 text-sm text-muted"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 bg-purple-500 rounded-full shrink-0"></span>{b}</li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-sm text-cyan-300 mb-3">Agent-Ready (ASO) — we implement it</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2">
            {['Machine-readable hours, geo coordinates and service menu deployed', 'Exact-price Offer markup deployed', 'Booking entry point published for agents (deep-linkable, pre-fillable)', 'Availability / next-available signal published and maintained', 'Verified profiles connected to your data', 'Reviews and ratings marked up'].map(b => (
              <li class="flex items-center gap-3 text-sm text-muted"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 bg-purple-500 rounded-full shrink-0"></span>{b}</li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Site Builds -->
    <div class="border-t border-white/5 pt-12">
      <div class="text-xs text-cyan-300 font-mono mb-2">ONE-TIME</div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-2">Site Builds & Migration</h2>
      <p class="text-muted mb-8 max-w-xl">Custom sites built on a global edge network — fast, modern, zero ongoing dev costs. Already have a site? We'll migrate it seamlessly. Every build includes:</p>
      <ul class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2 mb-8">
        {['Responsive design (mobile + desktop)', 'SEO-optimized from day one', 'SSL & global CDN included', 'Easy content management', '1 round of revisions included'].map(b => (
          <li class="flex items-center gap-3 text-sm text-muted"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 bg-purple-500 rounded-full shrink-0"></span>{b}</li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <div class="space-y-3">
        {[
          { pages: 'Landing Page — $1,250', desc: 'Single-page site. Perfect for product launches, lead gen, or a simple web presence.' },
          { pages: 'Up to 5 Pages — $2,500', desc: 'Home, About, Services, Blog, Contact. The full business stack.' },
          { pages: 'Site Migration — $1,000', desc: 'Moving from Wix, Squarespace, WordPress? We handle DNS, content, and redirects with zero downtime.' },
          { pages: '6+ Pages — Custom Quote', desc: "Complex sites, e-commerce, dashboards, or anything custom. Let's talk." },
        ].map((tier) => (
          <div class="gradient-border rounded-xl p-4">
            <div class="font-semibold text-sm">{tier.pages}</div>
            <div class="text-xs text-muted mt-1">{tier.desc}</div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="text-center pb-20 px-6">
  <p class="text-sm text-muted">
    <a href="/faq" class="text-cyan-400 hover:underline">Have questions? Read our FAQ →</a>
    &nbsp;·&nbsp;
    <a href="/about" class="text-cyan-400 hover:underline">Learn about the team behind Rank Labs →</a>
  </p>
</div>

</Layout>
